    "issue_alignment": "Public description: 'A vulnerability exists due to missing checks on string lengths when using strncmp for minimum bounds.' In armor_str_to_data_type, strncmp(str, \"BEGIN PGP MESSAGE\", len) compares only len attacker-controlled bytes; a 1-byte header 'B' is accepted as PGP_ARMORED_MESSAGE, producing a 1-byte param->armorhdr that later underflows stlen - 5 in armor_read_trailer, causing an out-of-bounds memcpy."
